PROCEDURE (the gpudyn3 acceptance harness, /tmp staging, sm_75 binary)
  BIN=$PWD/GPU2/run_turing/nbody7b.mpi-gpu \
      bash mpi_design/poc_validation/run_equiv.sh /tmp/nb7_turing_equiv
  NOTE: BIN was set EXPLICITLY. The harness auto-detect
  `ls GPU2/run_*/nbody7b.mpi-gpu | head -1` resolves to run_ampere/ (sm_86,
  the gpudyn3 build) alphabetically -- that binary aborts with "no kernel
  image is available for execution on the device" on the sm_75 2080s.
  run_equiv.sh: per-rank dirs, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1, NBODY_RANK0_IO=0, np 1/2/4,
  13049-body BSE input_short to END RUN; ICs from test_cpu_with_bse.

RESULT 1 -- rank->device binding (lrank % nGPU, nGPU = 2), from per-rank err.out
  np1  rank0 -> device 0
  np2  rank0 -> device 0   rank1 -> device 1          <- TWO DISTINCT GPUs
  np4  rank0 -> device 0   rank1 -> device 1
       rank2 -> device 0   rank3 -> device 1          <- exactly r % 2
  Every rank reports "#CPU 1, #GPU 1" (bound to ONE device, not all), and
  "device N: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080" naming the actual cudaSetDevice target
  (cudaGetDeviceProperties on the bound id -- stronger than an nvidia-smi
  snapshot). Irregular pair = "Opening GPUIRR lib. CPU ver." (the portable
  auto-vectorized default since d650b2f; AVX-512 on the Xeon Silver).

RESULT 2 -- correctness (run_equiv.sh bit-identity check)
  >>> PASS: bit-identical across np 1/2/4
  ADJUST/END-RUN physics (WTIME/CPUTOT/WTOT stripped) byte-identical for
  np2_rank{0,1} and np4_rank{0,1,2,3} vs the np1_rank0 reference. Splitting
  the regular force across the two physical 2080s (rank1/3 compute their
  j-slice on device 1) reproduces the single-GPU answer EXACTLY -- expected,
  because the two devices are the same sm_75 part (identical kernel
  summation) and the Allgatherv reduction is rank-ordered/deterministic.

CAVEATS / NOTES
  - GPUs read 0% util in nvidia-smi polling: input_short is a short run and
    the per-rank kernel bursts are sub-second on a 2080; the binding is proven
    by the deterministic device-name print, not by catching the processes.
  - Cross-arch bit-identity is NOT expected or claimed: an A40 (sm_86) build
    and a 2080 (sm_75) build differ in the last bits (different kernel
    summation), per 02_integration_serial_trim.md -- agreement there is
    physics-level. This log establishes np-invariance ON THIS HOST.
  - Two mpi-gpu binaries coexist in the tree (run_ampere sm_86, run_turing
    sm_75). Always pass BIN explicitly on gpudyn1.

STATUS: multi-GPU placement endgame (Path B G0) VERIFIED. Roadmap NEXT:
